          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "The 13½-inch-thick acrylic oculus lens beneath the 500,000 gallon Gulf Stream Aquarium at the Frost Museum of Science provides an underwater view of the re-created ocean off shore of South Florida.  The scalloped hammerhead shark (Sphyrna lewini) in the center swims above a lesser devil ray (Mobula hypostoma) swooping in on the left—with another ray up near the surface on the right.\n<p>On Google Earth:\n</p>\nFrost Science Museum  25°47'6.53\"N, 80°11'16.06\"W",
